{
  "title": "Decompose ramekin-core parser god-files (extract.rs, \
ingredient_parser.rs)",
  "description": "ramekin-core/src/extract.rs (~4,850 lines) and \
ramekin-core/src/ingredient_parser.rs (~4,700 lines) are the critical path for \
recipe quality and the riskiest files to touch. extract.rs interleaves \
JSON-LD, microdata, and blog/HTML-fallback extraction strategies plus image \
and footnote handling; ingredient_parser.rs has 50+ helper functions for \
amounts, units, parentheticals, and item splitting. Each has ~70 inline \
#[test] blocks mixed through the logic.\n\
\n\
Split by strategy/concern into submodules (e.g. \
extract/{jsonld,microdata,blog,images}.rs; \
ingredient_parser/{amounts,units,parentheticals,item}.rs), moving tests \
alongside their modules. Pure code motion — behavior must not change.\n\
\n\
Verification is the important part: `make pipeline` must produce an EMPTY \
data/ diff (any snapshot change means behavior changed), and all existing \
tests must pass unchanged. Doing this before the next wave of parsing fixes \
(see pipeline audit queue issues) makes those fixes safer and more reviewable.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
